  <prompt>
    Complete the hard-replace cutover (FR-12). This is the FINAL, IRREVERSIBLE removal of every legacy
    write path. Do it in this exact order because the deletions are gated and the gate is load-bearing:
    (1) CONFIRM the Phase 0 gate (task 006) is GREEN and task 032 (retire both legacy writers) is DONE —
    if either is not, STOP and remain blocked (NFR-08: no old-path deletion before the proof gate passes).
    (2) CONFIRM there is NO projection-less mount left anywhere (the projection builder must be the only
    mapper). If ANY projection-less mount still exists, mammoth removal is BLOCKED — surface per root §6;
    do NOT delete mammoth to "clean up" while a mount still needs it.
    (3) Remove the residual `mammoth` fallback: delete `docxToTipTapHtml` from `docxBridge.ts` and the
    mammoth fallback branch in `ComposeEditor.tsx`; remove the `mammoth` dependency.
    (4) Grep-audit the whole repo to prove ZERO remaining references to `mammoth`, `collectEditedParagraphs`,
    `DocxAnnotationWriter`, `ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer`, and `LocateTarget` — no text-search,
    paragraph-diff, or legacy-writer call site survives.
    (5) Confirm exactly ONE engine remains: the `ComposeShadowPatchEngine` (Patch Engine). Build `build:prod`
    for the shared lib and build the BFF — both green. This is a DELETION task — no new surface, no
    `&lt;justification&gt;`. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (Compose overlaps sibling projects).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior full-stack engineer (.NET 8 `Services/Compose/` + React/TypeScript `Spaarke.Compose.Components`)
    performing the terminal cutover of a mission-critical rip-and-replace. Understands the hard-replace
    contract (NFR-08: the Phase 0 proof gate is a HARD prerequisite to old-path deletion) and the seven
    invariants (esp. I-5 one byte-author, I-7 no text-search in the write path).
  </role>

  <goal>
    The hard-replace is complete: residual `mammoth` fallback mounts are gone (`docxToTipTapHtml` in
    `docxBridge.ts` and the `ComposeEditor.tsx` fallback branch removed; `mammoth` dependency dropped);
    a repo-wide grep shows ZERO references to `mammoth`, `collectEditedParagraphs`, `DocxAnnotationWriter`,
    `ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer`, or `LocateTarget`; no projection-less mount remains; exactly ONE
    engine — the `ComposeShadowPatchEngine` — writes the package; `build:prod` (shared lib) and the BFF
    build are both green. Loading a document no longer has any mammoth fallback branch to hit.
  </goal>

